WEBVTT

00:00:59.347 --> 00:01:01.149
It was practically a religious event.

00:01:01.173 --> 00:01:03.760
And this is when the Americans
beat the Russians,

00:01:03.784 --> 00:01:06.023
and this was --
yes, it was technically a game.

00:01:06.047 --> 00:01:07.374
Hockey is a game.

00:01:07.398 --> 00:01:09.144
But really, was this a game?

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:10.907
I mean, people cried.

00:01:10.931 --> 00:01:14.272
I've never seen my mother cry
like that at the end of Monopoly.

00:01:14.296 --> 00:01:15.438
(Laughter)

00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:17.814
And so this was an amazing experience.

00:01:17.838 --> 00:01:20.348
Or, if anybody here is from Boston --

00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:23.425
So when the Boston Red Sox
won the World Series

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:26.356
after I believe, 351 years --

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.657
(Laughter)

00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:29.940
when they won the World Series,
it was amazing.

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:32.362
I happened to be living
in Springfield at the time,